          "heading": "Unit-level design studio",
          "content": "In **Biomaterial selection and structure\u2013property relationships**, work with a fictional candidate material; do not perform human-use experiments. Choose a concrete intended function and list three nonnegotiable requirements. Select one property measurement, one mechanistic test and one control able to reveal a confounder. When there is insufficient evidence to select a material, explicitly state the missing test and its decision threshold. Maintain an evidence ledger separating literature-supported principles, calculated synthetic values and unresolved empirical claims. In this unit the corresponding numerical models are intentionally simple: they explore two selected dependencies, not a fully coupled human-system response.",
